{"kind":"article","sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ScreenClipKit"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Attaching your own files"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/attachingyourownfiles"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/AttachingYourOwnFiles","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your app knows things ScreenClip can’t see: the signed-in account, what’s in the cart, which feature flags are on, the last request the backend answered. Register an attachment provider and its files travel with every report, next to the built-in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/Diagnostics","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"code":["#if DEBUG","ScreenClipKit.setAttachmentProvider(\"cart\") { context in","  let cart = await MainActor.run { CartStore.shared.snapshot }  \/\/ any Encodable","  return [try .json(cart, name: \"cart\", summary: \"the cart's \\(cart.items.count) items and promo codes\")]","}","#endif"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The agent reads each file’s name and summary in its prompt. It opens a file only when the screenshot and note aren’t enough, so write the summary for it: say what is inside."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Attachment providers were added after ScreenClipKit 1.1.0. Use a newer package release or a revision that includes the attachment API."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"When the provider runs","anchor":"When-the-provider-runs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach logs and diagnostics"}]},{"type":"text","text":" enabled, the provider starts when the report sheet opens. It can read the app state while the tester annotates. Turning diagnostics on later starts a fresh provider run with the same report ID and capture time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Send"}]},{"type":"text","text":", ScreenClip waits up to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timeout"},{"type":"text","text":" more (5 seconds by default, at most 30) with "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Saving report…"}]},{"type":"text","text":" on screen. It then sends the report without whatever hasn’t arrived."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The provider runs off the main actor. Read main-actor state with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await MainActor.run { … }"},{"type":"text","text":", and keep heavy work out of that closure."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Several files, async work, and context","anchor":"Several-files-async-work-and-context"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A provider returns any number of attachments. Return an empty array to add nothing this time."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["ScreenClipKit.setAttachmentProvider(\"account\", timeout: .seconds(10)) { context in","  let session = await MainActor.run { Session.current }","  guard let session else { return [] }","  let flags = try await FeatureFlags.shared.current()","  APILog.shared.mark(\"ScreenClip report \\(context.reportID)\")","  return [","    try .json(session.debugSummary, name: \"account\", summary: \"signed-in account, plan, and region\"),","    .text(flags.description, name: \"feature-flags\", summary: \"remote feature flags in effect\"),","    .text(await APILog.shared.recent(20), name: \"api-requests\", summary: \"last 20 backend requests and status codes\"),","  ]","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipReportContext","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" carries the report’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reportID"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capturedAt"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenTitle"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenPath"},{"type":"text","text":". Log the report id next to your own records, such as a backend request id or an analytics session, to tie them to the report."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Cancellation and failure","anchor":"Cancellation-and-failure"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The provider is cancelled when the tester cancels the report, or turns off "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach logs and diagnostics"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Use cancellable APIs or check "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task.isCancelled"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the provider throws or misses its timeout, only its own files are left out. The report is still sent, and a line is logged under the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenClipKit"},{"type":"text","text":" subsystem."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Registering and removing","anchor":"Registering-and-removing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each id holds one provider. Registering the same id again replaces it, so calling "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" from an initializer or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onAppear"},{"type":"text","text":" is safe. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" removes it. Providers run concurrently, and their files are listed in registration order."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Names-and-limits","level":3,"text":"Names and limits"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes a file name the Mac accepts. It is lowercased, anything other than letters, digits, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes "},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and it is cut to 32 characters, plus "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".txt"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":".json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A name already in use, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"logs.txt","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or another provider’s, gets "},{"code":"-2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"-3","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and so on."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each attachment can be up to 1 MB (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumBytes","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"). Larger ones are left out."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All files in a report share a 4 MB limit. When a report is over it, the largest files are dropped first.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"What-not-to-attach","level":3,"text":"What not to attach"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Don’t attach secrets. On the Mac, token-like strings are hidden in text files, but JSON files are stored as sent. Any attached file can be read by an agent working on the report."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In Release builds ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" does nothing, and the closure is never called. Keep the call inside "},{"code":"#if DEBUG","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" anyway, so the code that gathers the data stays out of Release too.","type":"text"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add your app’s own state to every report, so the agent sees what the screenshot can’t show."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Attaching your own data","generated":true,"anchor":"Attaching-your-own-data","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipReportContext"]}],"references":{"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachment":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A file your app adds to a report, next to ScreenClip’s own logs and diagnostics."}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachment","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipAttachment"}],"title":"ScreenClipAttachment","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipAttachment"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit":{"images":[{"type":"icon","identifier":"screenclip-icon.svg"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Report what you see in your own iOS app, straight into ScreenClip on your Mac, where a coding agent fixes it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit","title":"ScreenClipKit","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipReportContext":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipReportContext"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What a provider knows about the report it is attaching to."}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipreportcontext","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipReportContext"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipReportContext","title":"ScreenClipReportContext","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipKit/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipkit\/removeattachmentprovider(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stops adding the files from the provider registered with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"removeAttachmentProvider","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"removeAttachmentProvider(_:)"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachment/maximumBytes":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachment\/maximumbytes","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumBytes"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumBytes","title":"maximumBytes","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The largest attachment ScreenClip sends. Larger ones are left out of the report.","type":"text"}]},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipKit/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipkit\/setattachmentprovider(_:timeout:_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Adds your app’s own files to every report: state, records, anything an agent would want"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to see next to the screenshot."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"setAttachmentProvider","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timeout","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13ScreenClip